      "The highlight of the expedition is reaching Everest Base Camp (5,364 m / 17,598 ft), where mountaineers prepare for their ascent of the world's highest mountain. The adventure continues with a hike to Kala Patthar (5,545 m / 18,192 ft), where you'll witness breathtaking close-up views of Mount Everest, along with Lhotse, Nuptse, Pumori, Ama Dablam, and the surrounding Himalayan peaks.",
