          "Today, we will take an early morning flight to Lukla, departing either from Kathmandu or Ramechhap, depending on the flight schedule. Widely regarded as one of the most scenic mountain flights in the world, the journey offers breathtaking views of lush valleys, terraced hillsides, and the snow-capped Himalayan range. As we approach Lukla, we will experience an exciting landing at the famous Tenzing-Hillary Airport, known for its short uphill runway nestled amidst the mountains.\n\nAfter arriving in Lukla, we will meet our local support team and complete the final trek preparations. You can also use this time to do any last-minute shopping or withdraw cash from one of the ATMs, as these facilities are limited further along the trail. We will then freshen up, enjoy a light snack, and begin our trek towards Phakding.\n\nThe trail is mostly downhill, passing through traditional Sherpa villages, colourful prayer flags, mani stones, and our first suspension bridge over the Dudh Koshi River. By afternoon, we will reach Phakding and check into our tea house, where we will unwind and prepare for the exciting days ahead.",
