        description:
          "Today, we will continue our journey towards Namche Bazaar, the gateway to the Everest region. The trail follows the Dudh Koshi River through beautiful pine forests and traditional Sherpa villages, crossing several suspension bridges along the way.\n\nWe will enter Sagarmatha National Park at Monjo, where our permits will be checked before continuing to Jorsalle, the last village before Namche Bazaar. We will stop here for lunch, as there are no tea houses or food stops until we reach Namche Bazaar.\n\nAfter lunch, we will cross the Dudh Koshi River and walk along the river for a while before beginning the day's most challenging climb. Along the way, we will pass the famous Hillary Suspension Bridge, one of the most photographed landmarks on the Everest Base Camp trail. As we continue climbing, we will be rewarded with stunning views of the surrounding valleys and, on a clear day, our first glimpse of Mount Everest.\n\nWe will reach Namche Bazaar by late afternoon and check into our tea house. Once you had some rest, take some time to explore the streets of Namche, visit the local cafés and bakeries, or browse the nearby shops. With its beautiful mountain views and lively atmosphere, Namche Bazaar is one of the highlights of the Everest Base Camp trek and a great place to spend the evening before tomorrow's acclimatization hike.",
